<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><span class="gr">$</span> ./gm-multimanager --about</div>
  <h1>gm-multiManager.<br><span class="accent">One assistant, several Google accounts.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">A personal tool I built and run on my own Mac. It gives Claude Code access to Gmail, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides and Calendar across the Google accounts I own, so one assistant can search, read and organize all of them.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="legal">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul class="proof-list">
      <li><strong>Gmail:</strong> search, read, label, archive and filter mail. It has no permanent-delete tool.</li>
      <li><strong>Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides:</strong> search, read, create and edit files. Files can be moved to Drive's trash, never permanently deleted.</li>
      <li><strong>Calendar:</strong> list, create, update and delete events. Guests are emailed only when I ask for it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul class="proof-list">
      <li>Runs locally as an MCP server on my Mac. Nothing is hosted and there's no backend.</li>
      <li>Google OAuth refresh tokens are stored in the macOS login Keychain.</li>
      <li>It acts only when I give Claude an instruction in my own session.</li>
      <li>The source is public: <a href="https://github.com/pravinemani5545/skills-and-mcp/tree/main/mcp/gmail-organizer-mcp">github.com/pravinemani5545/skills-and-mcp</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>Personal use only. It isn't offered as a service, and the only Google accounts connected to it are mine.</p>

    <p class="meta"><a href="/tools/gm-multimanager/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> · <a href="/tools/gm-multimanager/terms/">Terms of service</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
